### LedgerFlow — REST Client collection (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client compatible)
### Run `docker compose up`, then get a token, then run the requests below top to bottom.

@keycloakUrl = http://localhost:8180
@accountUrl = http://localhost:8081
@settlementUrl = http://localhost:8082
@queryUrl = http://localhost:8083

### 1. Get an access token (Keycloak, resource-owner password grant, demo realm/user)
# @name login
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/ledgerflow/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ledgerflow-demo&username=demo&password=demo

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. Create a payer account
# @name createPayer
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": "alice",
  "currency": "USD"
}

###
@payerId = {{createPayer.response.body.id}}

### 3. Create a payee account
# @name createPayee
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": "bob",
  "currency": "USD"
}

###
@payeeId = {{createPayee.response.body.id}}

### 4. Create a funding account and seed the payer (demonstrates Idempotency-Key)
# @name createFunding
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": "system-funding",
  "currency": "USD"
}

###
@fundingId = {{createFunding.response.body.id}}

### 5. Seed the payer with 200.00 (Idempotency-Key required on every mutating call)
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: seed-demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{fundingId}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "amount": "200.00",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "seed"
}

### 6. Replay the exact same request with the SAME Idempotency-Key: applies exactly once,
###    returns the original transfer, does NOT move money a second time.
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: seed-demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{fundingId}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "amount": "200.00",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "seed"
}

### 7. Reusing the SAME key with a DIFFERENT body: rejected with 409 Conflict
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: seed-demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{fundingId}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "amount": "999.00",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "seed"
}

### 8. A normal transfer, payer -> payee
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{payeeId}}",
  "amount": "25.00",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "lunch"
}

### 9. Missing Idempotency-Key header: rejected with 400
POST {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{payeeId}}",
  "amount": "5.00",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "no key"
}

### 10. Get account balance
GET {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{payerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Get ledger entries for the payer
GET {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{payerId}}/ledger-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Reconciliation: cached balance vs. ledger-derived balance
GET {{accountUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{payerId}}/reconcile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Create+execute a 2-way settlement (bill split) via settlement-service
# @name settlement
POST {{settlementUrl}}/api/v1/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payerAccountId": "{{payerId}}",
  "currency": "USD",
  "reason": "dinner split",
  "payees": [
    { "payeeAccountId": "{{payeeId}}", "amount": "10.00" }
  ]
}

###
@settlementId = {{settlement.response.body.id}}

### 14. Get settlement status
GET {{settlementUrl}}/api/v1/settlements/{{settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Read-model: balance projection (eventually consistent via Kafka)
GET {{queryUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{payerId}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Read-model: statement history
GET {{queryUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{payerId}}/statement
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Read-model: settlement audit trail
GET {{queryUrl}}/api/v1/settlements/{{settlementId}}/audit-trail
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
